    perf: gzip and cache headers in the install guide's nginx block (#1181)
    
    `install-guid.md` §8 is the only copy of the nginx site this project ships —
    there is no `deploy/nginx/` directory in the repository — so it is the config
    every operator pastes into `/etc/nginx/sites-available/`. It carried neither
    compression nor cache headers.
    
    Three changes, all inside that one `server { … }` block:
    
    - gzip at server level (gzip_vary on, comp_level 5, min_length 1024). The
      `gzip_types` list deliberately omits `font/woff2`: woff2 is already
      compressed, so gzipping it only burns CPU.
    - `location ^~ /build/assets/` — Vite emits content-hashed filenames there,
      so the content never changes under the same URL: a single
      `Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable` with `always`, and
      NO `expires` (the two together emit two Cache-Control headers).
    - `location ~* ^/(?:js|css|icons|fonts)/` — these paths are NOT hashed, so a
      deploy can replace their content under the same URL: `expires 1d`, and no
      `immutable`.
    
    Both static-asset locations REPEAT `X-Content-Type-Options` and
    `X-Frame-Options`. `add_header` does not inherit: a location that declares
    its own `add_header` drops every `add_header` of the enclosing server block,
    so without the repetition the assets would ship with no security headers at
    all — and the PHP SecurityHeaders middleware cannot cover them, because they
    never pass through PHP.
    
    The guide now says, next to the config, that the change only takes effect
    once the operator reloads nginx.
    
    `tests/Feature/InstallGuideNginxConfigTest.php` locks all of it against the
    shipped text: gzip is on, the hashed location exists, `immutable` appears
    nowhere else, `expires` is absent from the hashed location, and both security
    headers are repeated inside each location that declares an `add_header`.

